hw/con/ - board constraint files
================================

Xilinx XDC PHYSICAL constraints only (pins, I/O standards, config), one per
supported board. scr/{synth,build,timing,fmax}.tcl pick the file matching
BOARD.

    nexys_a7.xdc    Digilent Nexys 4 DDR / Nexys A7 (Artix-7 XC7A100T)
    basys3.xdc      Digilent Basys 3                (Artix-7 XC7A35T)

Each maps: clk, the reset push button (btn_rst), the USB-UART pins
(uart_rx_i / uart_tx_o) and four status LEDs.

ALL timing (the clock period, the async-I/O false paths, and the ALU
datapath's multicycle-path exception) lives in ../scr/constraints.tcl, NOT
here — it is board-independent and parameterised on the period, so the same
file drives synthesis, implementation and the Fmax sweep alike. Keeping it out
of the per-board XDC is deliberate: physical constraints are exactly the ones
that do NOT port across parts (the hard-coded-vs-queried DSP floorplan story
in doc/src/implementation.tex is a case in point), so they stay isolated here.

Default board is nexys_a7 (make bit BOARD=basys3 for the other).
